  "question": {
    "text": "The minimum energy required by a hydrogen atom in ground state to emit radiation in Balmer series is nearly :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For Balmer series, transition is from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>For transition to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, the minimum state to transition from is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. </p><p>Therefore, energy required <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Δ</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.1</mo><mi>eV</mi></math></p>"
  }
